        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3196b096-ad06-546e-9867-3838dcd21fea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ghosts, Battle for Haditha, The Hurt Locker, Redacted, Fair Game\n- People: Nick Broomfield, Kathryn Bigelow, Brian De Palma, Sean Penn\n- Concepts: Gweilo\n- Places: Jordan\n\nFacts:\n- The film Ghosts (2006) takes its title from the Cantonese slang term Gweilo (鬼佬), which means \"ghost man\" and is used for white people.\n- In its unmodified form, the term Gweilo applies only to people of European ethnicities and has a history of racially deprecatory use.\n- Battle for Haditha is Nick Broomfield's follow-up to Ghosts.\n- Battle for Haditha dramatizes real events using a documentary style.\n- Jordan was a shooting location for Battle for Haditha, The Hurt Locker, Redacted, and Fair Game.\n- The Hurt Locker was directed by Kathryn Bigelow.\n- Redacted was directed by Brian De Palma.\n- Fair Game starred Sean Penn.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a820f482-94ee-5740-b070-94b9bd3dd900",
        "text": "Page: Ghosts (2006 film). Sentence: The title is a reference to the Cantonese slang term \"Gweilo\" (鬼佬), meaning \"ghost man\", used for white people.\nPage: Gweilo. Sentence: In its unmodified form, it applies only to European ethnicities and has a history of racially deprecatory use.\nPage: Battle for Haditha. Sentence: Dramatising real events using a documentary style, \"Battle for Haditha\" is Broomfield's follow up to \"Ghosts.\"\nPage: Cinema of Jordan. Sentence: Recent films that were shot in Jordan are \"The Hurt Locker\" directed by Kathryn Bigelow, \"Redacted\" directed by Brian De Palma, some second unit scenes from \"\", \"Fair Game\" starring Sean Penn, and \"Battle for Haditha\" directed by Nick Broomfield.",
